"comparison": "Both companies identify generative AI as a key emerging technology driving demand for their products and services. However, their risk profiles regarding this trend differ significantly. NVDA discloses that while generative AI has driven increased data center demand, the long-term trajectory is unknown, and their demand estimates for such new use cases may be incorrect, creating revenue volatility. In contrast, AMD focuses on its strategic investments to support this demand by consolidating AI teams, improving its ROCm software ecosystem, and acquiring Silo AI to accelerate AI model deployment on its hardware, rather than highlighting uncertainty or volatility in that demand.",
