"relationship": "related_topic",
"comparison": "Both companies address the volatility and unpredictability associated with AI-driven demand. NVDA specifically warns that demand estimates for new use cases like generative AI can be incorrect, leading to revenue or supply level volatility. AVGO similarly lists 'anticipated or actual demand for AI-related products' as a key factor affecting its product demand. However, while NVDA frames this as a direct revenue risk due to estimation errors, AVGO categorizes it as one of several macro and operational factors (alongside customer loss and distributor inventory) influencing demand volume.",
