"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both NVDA and INTC explicitly discuss the risks associated with the rapid evolution of the AI market and the uncertainty of demand for AI capabilities. NVDA notes that while generative AI has recently driven demand, its 'long-term trajectory is unknown' and estimates may be incorrect. INTC faces similar uncertainty, stating that markets for AI products are 'rapidly evolving, are difficult to predict, and may impact demand,' citing shifts in customer spend toward GPUs as an example. Both companies acknowledge the difficulty in forecasting revenue from new AI use cases, though INTC highlights specific product-level failures (Gaudi inventory charges) while NVDA highlights the general risk of estimation errors.",
